+- id: R03
+  symptom: 'User risk table / G03 / G04: two runs overlap (same-minute second entity, or a Scheduler retry after a slow attempt) — shared staging
+    truncated, watermark advanced over lost rows, or the second entity 429s out'
+  layer: L15
+  surfaces: A (B2 C need their own guard)
+  cause: 'main.py used one shared new_deals_staging with WRITE_TRUNCATE and both jobs had cron "0 7 * * 1"; --max-instances 1 --concurrency 1
+    alone does not serialise a retry after a 504 and turns the second job into 429s (G04 contested: the retry race needs a > 540 s run, unrealistic
+    at ~6 deals/week; the 429 starvation is real).'
+  fix: 'Per-run staging new_deals_staging_<entity>_<run_ts> (merge_rows), report_state.lock_until lease via one atomic UPDATE (acquire_lease →
+    409), offset schedules SCHEDULE_ICALPS="20 7 * * 1"; the instance cap stays as defence in depth. B2: N8N_CONCURRENCY_PRODUCTION_LIMIT=1 +
+    maxScale 1 + respond-when-finished; C: transaction + value-idempotent PATCH.'
+  verified: fixed in main.py (tests/test_main_offline.py::test_live_uses_per_run_staging_and_frozen_update_list, ::test_overlapping_run_gets_409_and_writes_nothing);
+    deploy/n8n/service.yaml; sql/new_deals_weekly.sql
